cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "schellingChords: a sonified Schelling segregation model over chord voicings"
abstract: >-
  A Mesa agent-based model that runs a one-dimensional Schelling segregation
  process in which the agents are chords occupying the beats of a 4/4 window,
  and sonifies the segregation as it unfolds. A chord is satisfied when the
  mean Jaccard distance of its pitch-class set to its occupied neighbours falls
  within tolerance; unsatisfied chords relocate to a random vacant slot.
authors:
